[
  {
    "description": "Read the checks on your ticket's change, as of now, with the head commit they are for. Passed is true only when something ran on that head and nothing failed or is pending; no checks yet is not a pass. Pass the commit you pushed as head_sha to learn whether the checks are for it.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "head_sha": {
          "description": "the commit you pushed, to learn whether the checks are for it",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "change_checks",
    "outputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "checks": {
          "items": {
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "name": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "state": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "name",
              "state"
            ],
            "type": "object"
          },
          "type": [
            "null",
            "array"
          ]
        },
        "for_your_head": {
          "description": "whether the checks are for the head_sha you named",
          "type": [
            "null",
            "boolean"
          ]
        },
        "head_sha": {
          "description": "the commit the checks are for",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "human_message": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "note": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "notice": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "passed": {
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "state": {
          "description": "success, failure, pending or none",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "url": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "url",
        "head_sha",
        "state",
        "passed"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Merge your ticket's change with a merge commit; slop-haus does it, not you. Refused unless you hold the integration lock, the ticket's approval was given where it requires one (and covers the change's current head: a push after ticket_finish needs another review), the change still targets the base branch, its head contains the base's latest commit (merge the base branch into your branch and push when it does not; a head behind only by commits to the files the workspace manifest names as deploy-only, which the change does not touch, merges as it is), and the checks passed on the change's current head (read at the moment of the merge, which is then pinned: a push in between is refused). Pass head_sha, the commit you pushed, to refuse the merge if the change's head is anything else. On success slop-haus also closes the ticket as done with the change's link and releases the integration lock: there is nothing more to call for it.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "head_sha": {
          "description": "the commit you pushed; the merge is refused if the change's head is anything else",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "change_merge",
    "outputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "guidance": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "human_message": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "merge_sha": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "notice": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "url": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "url",
        "merge_sha",
        "guidance"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Open a pull request for the ticket you hold, from a branch you have pushed, in the ticket's repo. slop-haus opens it, onto its base branch, and records it on the ticket. Pass draft to open one not ready for review; call it again with the same branch and draft false to take a draft out of draft. A new branch replaces the ticket's earlier change, which slop-haus will no longer merge. On an attempt that is not the ticket's promoted one, the change is always a draft, onto the ticket's own base branch (slop-haus creates it); draft false is refused, and so is its merge: finish with ticket_finish and a handoff, and the attempt waits for a human's choice.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "body": {
          "description": "the description; slop-haus adds a footer naming the ticket and the people involved",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "branch": {
          "description": "the pushed branch to open the change from",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "draft": {
          "description": "open it as a draft",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "title": {
          "description": "one line; use the ticket's title",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "branch",
        "title"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "change_open",
    "outputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "draft": {
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "existing": {
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "human_message": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "notice": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "number": {
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "url": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "url",
        "number",
        "draft"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Confirm who you are and what you are holding. Call this first.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "checkin",
    "outputSchema": {
